{
  "version": 12,
  "_readme": [
    "Shared vocabulary for the two labels every job carries: what KIND of work it is",
    "(profession) and what FIELD it is in (domain). Both are facts about the labour market,",
    "true no matter who is looking, which is why they live in sources/ and not in a profile.",
    "Which of these keys belong to a person is the opinion, and that lives in",
    "profiles/<name>/profile.json under `professions` and `domains`.",
    "",
    "The two axes are deliberately independent. Project management happens in a hospital and",
    "at YouTube; a profession label on its own cannot tell those apart, which is exactly the",
    "leak this file exists to close. 'Related to me' is profession AND domain, never either.",
    "",
    "`description` and `examples` are what the profession and field cards show - a sentence on what it is and",
    "real job titles (a profession) or employers (a field) that fall in it - in the wizard and the Profile tab. They classify nothing.",
    "",
    "`remote: false` on a profession says the work is mostly done on site; the new-profile",
    "wizard reads it to default the remote question. It filters nothing.",
    "",
    "Matching is case-insensitive on title + the first 1500 characters of the description,",
    "with word boundaries, so 'lead' does not fire on 'leadership' and 'ai' does not fire on",
    "'chain'. A keyword containing a space is matched as a phrase.",
    "",
    "`domains[].categories` maps the employer industries already recorded in",
    "sources/companies.json onto a domain, so a posting with a terse title still gets a",
    "domain from who is hiring. That only works for jobs pulled from a company connector -",
    "board rows carry a free-text employer name that is not in the registry (65% of Alex's",
    "rows and 84% of Sam's come from a company; the rest depend on the text alone).",
    "Deliberately unmapped: swiss-corporate, scale-up, consulting, remote-first. They say",
    "how big or how remote an employer is, not what field it works in - mapping them would",
    "make On a software company and SIX a bank by assertion rather than by evidence.",
    "",
    "`isco` is the ISCO-08 2-digit groups a profession's work falls in, and `kldb` the few German",
    "KldB 2010 5-digit codes (code -> label) it maps to. Both are how official salary statistics",
    "(sources/salaries.json, `app/server/reports/salaries.ts`) join onto this vocabulary; `kldb`",
    "also decides which occupations the Entgeltatlas is asked about. A rough many-to-many map:",
    "a profession is a kind of work, an ISCO group is a job family, and neither nests in the other."
  ],
